==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Octo Balloons are [[Monster Part]]s dropped by [[Octorok]]s. [[Link]], while using a [[Cooking Pot]], can cook Octo Balloons with critters such as [[Lizard]]s, [[Frog]]s, [[Insect]]s or [[Fairy|Fairies]] to make [[Elixir]]s. They can also be purchased for 20 [[Rupee]]s from [[Beedle]] at the [[Dueling Peaks Stable]] and [[Highland Stable]] or in [[Lurelin Village]] at the [[Merchant Boat]]. They can be sold to merchants or exchanged at the [[Fang and Bone]] for one [[Mon]] apiece. Octo Balloons can also be used as an ingredient for [[Purple Dye]] at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]].

Octo Balloons can be dropped and used to lift [[Object]]s such as a [[Barrel]]s or stone slabs.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> They can thus be used to solve simple puzzles or lift non-metallic Objects. [[Sky Octorok]]s use this property to lift wooden platforms, creating aerial fortresses for other [[Enemy|Enemies]].

During the "[[Balloon Flight]]" [[Side Quest]], a young girl named [[Shamae]] living at the [[Woodland Stable]] requires Link to use at least two Octo Balloons to lift a Barrel into the sky.<ref name="BotW Shamae"/> If Link is able to do this for her, she will give him a [[Star Fragment]] as a reward.<ref name="BotW Shamae 2"/>

